Some of the key commitments include the provision of food, investor partnerships, and UK-driving executives to "help children to develop in full", the promise to secure Rwanda $35 million to help avoid malnutrition in the country after receiving more than 4,700 tweets from citizens.
“With the support of the UK government, donors, national governments and citizens of different countries, we can eradicate the social injustice of malnutrition in history,” Ambassador Tracy Ulman said in April 2018.
In addition, the group reported that after more than 5,000 shares had been cunning in the UK to improve food for mothers and children, the government has announced the funding of the "food Assistance" project, which reaches 5 million women and children with food problems.
In response to one of the frequent questions on the site "what makes you think that we can end poverty?"
The Global Festiny replied: It will be a long and difficult path, sometimes we will suffer defeat and failure.
But, like great civil rights and movements against apartheid, we'll gain success because together we're stronger.
