He said: “I still believe that this feeling that you are not like everyone else and insignificant was what gave me strength and inspiration for success.””
He wanted to prove that he was "someone", he said that he would not disappoint those who learned about his sexuality.
Twi-time Bronze Olympiad medalist has become a significant activist of the LGBT movement and at the Commonwealth Games in Australia this year has urged countries not to criminalize homosexuals.
He said that he expressed his opinion, because he was lucky enough to live openly, without persecutions and wanted to give "hope" to others.
