“Red Tide” information: Concentration is decreasing in Pinella, Monati and Sarasota
The newest report from the Florida Preservation Committee of fish and wild animals shows a general decline in the concentration of "red tide" in some parts of Tampa Bey.
According to the Committee's information, it is reported about certain flowering places in the areas of Pinelos, Monati, Sarasota, Charlotte and Kalie, which means a decrease in concentration.
The flowering "red tide" stretches for approximately 130 miles (200 km) of the coastline from the northern part of Pinelos County to the southern part of Lee County.
Pieces of flowering can be found at a distance of about 10 miles (15 km) from the coast in the Hilzbar County, but compared to last week their number is decreasing.
"Red Bowl" was also seembled in Paska district.
Medium-size concentration on the shore or near the shore in Pinelas County was observed last weest, in Hielsborough concentration was from low-to-haire. In Monati about the background to a tall, on the shore or close shore in Sarotogo County, the concentration was from background to high, in Charlotte County to the middle, on the shore or close shore in Lee County to a high-end and in Kalje County low concentration.
The irrigation of the respiratory tracks was reported from the districts of Pinelas, Monatti, Sarasota, Lee and Kallier.
Last week there were no reports of irritation of respiratory tracks from North-Western Florida.
